,"kind":"gbp"}]}},"dossier":{"summary":null,"compliance":null,"documents":[{"title":"FRS-WS-26-003-Annual-Treasury-Management-and-Financial-Resilience-Report-2025-to-2026","url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59049/frs-ws-26-003-annual-treasury-management-and-financial-resil.pdf","committee":"Performance and Audit Scrutiny Committee","date":"23/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"FRS-WS-26-004-Treasury-Management-Report-June-2026","url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59050/frs-ws-26-004-treasury-management-report-june-2026.pdf","committee":"Performance and Audit Scrutiny Committee","date":"23/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"FRS-WS-26-004-Treasury-Management-Report-Appendix-1","url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59051/frs-ws-26-004-treasury-management-report-appendix-1.pdf","committee":"Performance and Audit Scrutiny Committee","date":"23/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"FRS-WS-26-004-Treasury-Management-Report-Appendix-2","url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59052/frs-ws-26-004-treasury-management-report-appendix-2.pdf","committee":"Performance and Audit Scrutiny Committee","date":"23/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Part 2 - Article 14 - Suspension, Interpretation, Maintenance and Publication of the Constitution (April 2019)","url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s31626/part-2-article-14-suspension-interpretation-maintenance-and.pdf","committee":"West Suffolk Council Constitution","date":"08/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"Part 3 - Section 4 - Budget Setting and Medium Term Planning (April 2021)","url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s40425/part-3-section-4-budget-setting-and-medium-term-planning-apr.pdf","committee":"West Suffolk Council Constitution","date":"08/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"Part-4-Budget-and-Policy-Framework-Procedure-Rules-April-2025","url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s55137/part-4-budget-and-policy-framework-procedure-rules-april-202.pdf","committee":"West Suffolk Council Constitution","date":"08/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"CAB-WS-26-021-Appendix-2-Evaluation-Framework","url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s58370/cab-ws-26-021-appendix-2-evaluation-framework.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"19/05/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-10-06","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; *RESERVE DATE*","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-13","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-03","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-17","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; *RESERVE DATE*","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-21","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-23","committee":"Performance and Audit Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Performance and Audit Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"West Suffolk audit will remain qualified until 2027-28 due to \u00a37.8m in unaudited property assets","lead":"West Suffolk received a qualified audit opinion for 2024-25 \u2014 the auditor could not fully sign off the accounts \u2014 and another is expected for 2025-26. The qualification relates to property assets worth \u00a37.8 million last valued in 2022-23, which remain unaudited. These assets fall outside the council's current five-year revaluation programme and will not be revalued for some years; once they are, the accounts impact will take a further two years to flow through. Full audit clearance is not anticipated until 2027-28. This represents improvement from 2022-23 and 2023-24, when the national audit backlog left West Suffolk without any audit assurance. Reserves, another element of the qualification, can be resolved in the 2025-26 audit. The auditor found no concerns with the council's arrangements to manage money or decision-making properly.","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"6-PAS-WS-26-015-EY-Risk-Assessment-Update","paper_url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59460/59460.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"West Suffolk's audit qualification will persist until at least 2027 as \u00a37.8m of property assets await revaluation","lead":"West Suffolk Council received a qualified audit opinion for 2024-25, marking recovery from the nationwide local audit crisis that left the council's 2022-23 and 2023-24 accounts unaudited. However, external auditors Ernst & Young say the qualification cannot be lifted until property assets valued at \u00a37.8 million\u2014last assessed in 2022-23\u2014are revalued as part of the council's rolling five-year programme. Even once that revaluation occurs, a further two years must pass before the impact flows through the accounts and auditors can sign off in full. Auditors expect a clean conclusion on whether the council manages its money efficiently. The council signed its draft accounts for 2025-26 on 29 May, ahead of the statutory deadline, with a qualified opinion anticipated before the January 2027 backstop date.","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"6-PAS-WS-26-015-EY-Risk-Assessment-Update","paper_url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59460/59460.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Performance and Audit Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"8-PAS-WS-26-017-Annual-Governance-Statement-Appendix-A","paper_url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59480/59480.pdf","headline":"The council's wholly-owned housing company, Barley Homes Group Limited, received an unqualified audit opinion for 2024-2025.","detail":"External auditors reviewed Barley Homes (Group) Limited for 2024-2025 and found its financial statements compliant with Companies Act requirements. This stands in contrast to the qualified opinion on the parent council's accounts, indicating that the governance and accounting controls within the subsidiary are adequate.","category":"governance","matters":"The council's ability to use its housing company for housing delivery and economic development depends on sound controls and clean audit opinions. An unqualified opinion provides assurance that the subsidiary can function as intended despite audit issues in the parent council.","figures":"2024 to 2025","quote":"The audit found that the Company's financial statement provided a true and fair view of its affairs and was in accordance with the requirements of the Companies Act 2006.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Performance and Audit Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"8-PAS-WS-26-017-Annual-Governance-Statement-Appendix-A","paper_url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59480/59480.pdf","headline":"Government has withdrawn the decision to create three unitary authorities in Suffolk, removing a major structural change the council was planning for.","detail":"On 7 September 2026, the Secretary of State announced a review of local government reorganisation and withdrew the March 2026 decision that the council had been preparing for. The council had submitted a joint proposal with other Suffolk councils in September 2025 based on the then-stated government commitment to create three unitary authorities. While the government has re-stated commitment to future structural simplification, the timing and form are now uncertain.","category":"governance","matters":"Reorganisation would have had major implications for the council's funding, structure, and viability. Its withdrawal removes a defined planning assumption but leaves uncertainty about whether and when future restructuring might occur, affecting the council's strategic outlook and medium-term financial sustainability.","figures":"7 September 2026, March 2026, September 2025","quote":"government has withdrawn its decision made in March 2026 to create three new unitary authorities in Suffolk","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Performance and Audit Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"8-PAS-WS-26-017-Annual-Governance-Statement-Appendix-A","paper_url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59480/59480.pdf","headline":"The 2024-2025 accounts carry a qualified audit opinion due to unresolved issues from two years prior.","detail":"External auditors signed off the 2024-2025 accounts on 21 January 2026, ahead of the 27 February backstop date. However, a qualified opinion was issued rather than an unqualified one, because the 2022-2023 accounts had received a disclaimer of opinion (the most severe audit classification). This left insufficient audit evidence for the opening balances used in 2024-2025, preventing the auditors from verifying the current year's position against prior years.","category":"audit","matters":"A qualified audit opinion weakens lender confidence in the accuracy of the council's financial statements. The underlying cause \u2014 a prior-year disclaimer of opinion \u2014 indicates unresolved governance or financial reporting control issues.","figures":"21 January 2026, 27 February 2026","quote":"due to the disclaimer of opinion on the 2022 to 2023 accounts and the resultant lack of audit evidence for the opening balances for 2024 to 2025 a qualified opinion for the 2024 to 2025 accounts was issued.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Performance and Audit Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"9-PAS-WS-26-018-Annual-Statement-of-Accounts-Appendix-A","paper_url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59481/59481.pdf","headline":"Council assessed as going concern with sufficient liquidity for next 12 months and forecast cash balances of \u00a310m at March 2027.","detail":"The council confirmed going concern status based on: (a) robust current and forecast financial position; (b) balanced budgets set for 2026-27 and 2027-28; (c) \u00a36.13m General Fund and \u00a352.01m earmarked reserves; (d) cash flow modelling showing ability to work within Capital Financing Requirement without operational borrowing; (e) access to \u00a329.5m cash and short-term investments; (f) forecast \u00a310m cash at March 2027.","category":"governance","matters":"Going concern is foundational to all lending decisions. The council's formal assessment, with detailed supporting evidence on cash, reserves and budgeting, provides assurance on financial continuity.","figures":"\u00a329.5m cash and investments at 31 March 2026; \u00a310m forecast cash at March 2027; \u00a36.13m General Fund; \u00a352.01m earmarked reserves","quote":"Overall, based on its cash flow forecast, borrowing potential and access to investment funds, as well as the level of general fund and reserve balances it holds, the council determines that it has sufficient liquidity to continue to deliver services for the foreseeable future.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Performance and Audit Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"9-PAS-WS-26-018-Annual-Statement-of-Accounts-Appendix-A","paper_url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59481/59481.pdf","headline":"Government withdrew March 2026 decision to create three unitary authorities in Suffolk, creating strategic uncertainty.","detail":"On 7 September 2026, the Secretary of State announced withdrawal of the March 2026 decision to create three new unitary authorities in Suffolk following 'updated and privileged legal advice'. The government restated commitment to effective and sustainable local government and simplifying council structures. West Suffolk states it 'remains a high performing and ambitious council' and 'remains financially sound' despite this structural uncertainty.","category":"governance","matters":"Unitary authority creation would have triggered significant transition costs and restructuring. Withdrawal removes that immediate risk but creates uncertainty about future structure. Lenders need to know this is a managed strategic uncertainty, not a financial crisis.","figures":"Decision withdrawn 7 September 2026 (9 days before committee meeting date)","quote":"On 7 September 2026, the Secretary of State for Housing, Communities and Local Government announced that she would be reviewing the current plans for local government reorganisation in Suffolk, as well as other areas of the country, following 'updated and privileged legal advice'. As such, government has withdrawn its decision made in March 2026 to create three new unitary authorities in Suffolk.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-24"},"name":"West Suffolk","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-26","since_iso":"2026-08-27","distress":false,"headline":"The council's wholly-owned housing company, Barley Homes Group Limited, received an unqualified audit opinion for 2024-2025.","lead":"The council's ability to use its housing company for housing delivery and economic development depends on sound controls and clean audit opinions. An unqualified opinion provides assurance that the subsidiary can function as intended despite audit issues\u2026","also":["34 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Cabinet on 2026-10-06","n_findings":35,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"8-PAS-WS-26-017-Annual-Governance-Statement-Appendix-A","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.westsuffolk.gov.uk/documents/s59480/59480.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":94,"news_drafts_total":2}}